// `<...>` is a box. Without a mark it is a name tag, a label for the reader that
// means nothing to tomet; with a `?` it is a hole. A shape that is no box is text,
// and never an error.

Pass --out <PATH> to write the file, or open <ファイル> and Vec<T> instead.

Text that looks like a box and is not one: a < b, x<=1, <->, <!doctype html>,
</x>, <x/>, and a<b と c>d stay as written.

A hole in running text: adr-<?int(n)>-<?(slug)>.md

<?()>

<?(id)>[adr-<?int(n)>-<?(slug)>]

A hole takes args and options in its head, <?int(n){min: 1}>, and a matcher
may be namespaced, <?tandr.heading(h)>.

@card[
  <?(body)>
]
